UNION ALL SELECT 'Oliva', 'fr', 'histoire 1 (nouveau texte)', (LOCATE(CAST('L''histoire de la famille Oliva commence à Pinar del Río, à Cuba : selon la maison, Melanio Oliva y cultiva du tabac pour la première fois en 1886, interrompit ses cultures pour la guerre d''indépendance cubaine, puis les reprit. Son fils Facundo, dit la maison, prit la suite au début des années 1920 (Wikipédia nomme Hipolito).' AS BINARY), CAST(`history` AS BINARY)) > 0) FROM `brands` WHERE `name` = 'Oliva'
UNION ALL SELECT 'Oliva', 'fr', 'histoire 1 (ancien texte parti)', (LOCATE(CAST('L''histoire de la famille Oliva commence dans la province de Pinar del Río, à Cuba, en 1886 — quand elle planta pour la première fois du tabac à l''extrémité ouest de l''île, dans ce qu''on allait appeler la Vuelta Abajo. Pendant plus de soixante ans, les Oliva cultivèrent dans cette terre rouge, y acquérant le savoir que leurs descendants emporteraient en exil.' AS BINARY), CAST(`history` AS BINARY)) = 0) FROM `brands` WHERE `name` = 'Oliva'
UNION ALL SELECT 'Oliva', 'en', 'histoire 1 (nouveau texte)', (LOCATE(CAST('The history of the Oliva family begins in Pinar del Río, Cuba: according to the house, Melanio Oliva first grew tobacco there in 1886, interrupted his crops for the Cuban war of independence, then resumed them. His son Facundo, says the house, took over in the early 1920s (Wikipedia names Hipolito).

When Cuba changed regime, the grandson Gilberto Oliva moved from growing to tobacco brokerage. According to the house, he left the island in the early 1960s and looked in Honduras, Panama, Mexico and the Philippines for conditions close to the Cuban taste, before settling in Nicaragua. The dates differ: Wikipedia has him leave for Spain in 1964, grow in Nicaragua in 1969, then leave the country in 1979 and return in 1995.

For years the family was grower and broker, with no brand in its own name. His son José says that Gilberto senior grew tobacco every year and put it aside (trade press, December 2017). No page read names the manufacturers who bought.

In 1995, Gilberto Oliva and his son Gilberto Jr. made a cigar in the factory of Néstor Plasencia senior, in Honduras, which they named Gilberto Oliva; a year later they opened their own factory in Nicaragua and shortened the name to Oliva. The Serie V is the house''s flagship line; its year of launch differs between sources (2004 in the former profile, 2006 according to Wikipedia, June 2007 according to Halfwheel).

The family grows Cuban-seed tobacco in Nicaragua, says the house. In July 2016, Oliva Cigar Co. was bought by the Belgian group J. Cortès; in 2021, the trade press describes it as its subsidiary, the family remaining at the head of the company in Miami Lakes (Florida).

In 2023 Oliva opened the Black Swan series. The name belongs to the American retailer CigarPage, not to the house: every edition of the series is entrusted to a different factory and built on a particular lot of tobacco found there. The Oliva edition is rolled in Nicaragua, under a Connecticut Broadleaf wrapper, over an Ecuadorian binder and Nicaraguan filler. Rocky Patel, E.P. Carrillo and Joya de Nicaragua made the three that followed — all three in this atlas.

Oliva also rolls Rustico, for a single line, which the retailer Atlantic Cigar Company, launched in the late 1990s, sells under the name Rustico Habano. In October 2026, only the Reserve line is given there as made by Oliva, in Nicaragua: Ecuadorian Habano wrapper, Nicaraguan binder and filler, hand-rolled longfiller, in Gordo 4 x 60. The Habano line is given there as Dominican, with no factory named.' AS BINARY), CAST(`history_en` AS BINARY)) > 0) FROM `brands` WHERE `name` = 'Oliva'
UNION ALL SELECT 'Oliva', 'en', 'histoire 1 (ancien texte parti)', (LOCATE(CAST(CONCAT('The Oliva family story begins in Pinar del Río Province, Cuba, in 1886 — when the family first planted tobacco in the western end of the island that would become known as Vuelta Abajo. For over sixty years, the Olivas grew tobacco in that red soil, developing the cultivation knowledge that their descendants would carry into exile.', CHAR(13), '
', CHAR(13), '
When Oswaldo Oliva left Cuba after the revolution, he brought seeds, agricultural knowledge, and the understanding that good tobacco required specific conditions to express its quality. After periods in Honduras and Miami, he established plantations in Nicaragua''s Jalapa Valley in 1968 — a growing region where the combination of volcanic soil, altitude, and consistent humidity creates conditions that experienced tasters recognize as the closest analog to Vuelta Abajo outside Cuba.', CHAR(13), '
', CHAR(13), '
For nearly three decades, Oliva was the industry''s best-kept open secret. If you smoked a premium Nicaraguan or Honduran cigar between 1970 and 1995, there was a reasonable probability that the leaf in your hand had been grown on Oliva land and sold to the manufacturer who put their name on the band. Davidoff, Padrón, Ashton, and dozens of others sourced Oliva leaf. The family sold it without complaint and without publicity. They were growers, not brand builders.', CHAR(13), '
', CHAR(13), '
The third generation changed that calculation. In 1995, convinced that the family''s leaf quality deserved its own identity, they launched Oliva Cigars. The family''s structural advantage is ownership. Every leaf that goes into an Oliva cigar was grown on family-owned land in Jalapa or Estelí. Gilberto Oliva Jr. inspects his plantations personally, on horseback, every growing season. This connection between the family and the soil has produced a consistency of quality across three decades of commercial production that no contract-sourcing arrangement can match.

In 2023 Oliva opened the Black Swan series. The name belongs to the American retailer CigarPage, not to the house: every edition of the series is entrusted to a different factory and built on a particular lot of tobacco found there. The Oliva edition is rolled in Nicaragua, under a Connecticut Broadleaf wrapper, over an Ecuadorian binder and Nicaraguan filler. Rocky Patel, E.P. Carrillo and Joya de Nicaragua made the three that followed — all three in this atlas.

Oliva also rolls Rustico, for a single line, which the retailer Atlantic Cigar Company, launched in the late 1990s, sells under the name Rustico Habano. In October 2026, only the Reserve line is given there as made by Oliva, in Nicaragua: Ecuadorian Habano wrapper, Nicaraguan binder and filler, hand-rolled longfiller, in Gordo 4 x 60. The Habano line is given there as Dominican, with no factory named.') AS BINARY), CAST(`history_en` AS BINARY)) = 0) FROM `brands` WHERE `name` = 'Oliva'
UNION ALL SELECT 'Oliva', 'es', 'histoire 1 (nouveau texte)', (LOCATE(CAST('La historia de la familia Oliva empieza en Pinar del Río, en Cuba: según la casa, Melanio Oliva cultivó allí tabaco por primera vez en 1886, interrumpió sus cultivos por la guerra de independencia cubana y luego los retomó. Su hijo Facundo, dice la casa, tomó el relevo a principios de los años 1920 (Wikipedia nombra a Hipolito).' AS BINARY), CAST(`history_es` AS BINARY)) > 0) FROM `brands` WHERE `name` = 'Oliva'
UNION ALL SELECT 'Oliva', 'es', 'histoire 1 (ancien texte parti)', (LOCATE(CAST('La historia de la familia Oliva empieza en la provincia de Pinar del Río, en Cuba, en 1886 —cuando plantó por primera vez tabaco en el extremo occidental de la isla, en lo que se llamaría la Vuelta Abajo. Durante más de sesenta años, los Oliva cultivaron en esa tierra roja, adquiriendo allí el saber que sus descendientes se llevarían al exilio.' AS BINARY), CAST(`history_es` AS BINARY)) = 0) FROM `brands` WHERE `name` = 'Oliva'
UNION ALL SELECT 'Oliva', 'de', 'histoire 1 (nouveau texte)', (LOCATE(CAST('Die Geschichte der Familie Oliva beginnt in Pinar del Río auf Kuba: Laut dem Haus baute Melanio Oliva dort 1886 zum ersten Mal Tabak an, unterbrach seinen Anbau wegen des kubanischen Unabhängigkeitskrieges und nahm ihn dann wieder auf. Sein Sohn Facundo übernahm, sagt das Haus, Anfang der 1920er Jahre (Wikipedia nennt Hipolito).' AS BINARY), CAST(`history_de` AS BINARY)) > 0) FROM `brands` WHERE `name` = 'Oliva'
UNION ALL SELECT 'Oliva', 'de', 'histoire 1 (ancien texte parti)', (LOCATE(CAST('Die Geschichte der Familie Oliva beginnt 1886 in der Provinz Pinar del Río auf Kuba — als sie zum ersten Mal Tabak am westlichen Ende der Insel pflanzte, in dem, was man später Vuelta Abajo nennen sollte. Über sechzig Jahre lang bauten die Oliva auf dieser roten Erde an und erwarben dort das Wissen, das ihre Nachkommen ins Exil mitnehmen sollten.' AS BINARY), CAST(`history_de` AS BINARY)) = 0) FROM `brands` WHERE `name` = 'Oliva'
